:: Moving On
"$player.pref it is!"

"What is this place?" you ask

"Why Ostia, of course! The newest and finest luxury resortoid in the Redrock Family of Worlds." Benny scitters around in a circle, facing outward with its little claws splayed, as if to emcompass the landscape. "A thousand tomorrows, today!"

"Restortoid, huh? How did I get here?"

"What an odd question." Benny holds one claw to its mouth thoughtfully. "Do you not know?"

"That's why I'm asking."

"I simply found you here on the beach! I've been making the rounds, keeping an eye or two out for guests in need."

<ul class="player-options">
    <li>[['"So you just found me randomly."']]</li>
</ul>

:: "So you just found me randomly."

The crab shrugs. "I'm here to serve."

Great, they conked you on the head and left you on a spec planet. Nothing but a random wandering clippy droid to keep you company.

"If I may, $player.pref, you seem a bit disoriented. Do you have an emergency contact? Or may I lead you to the nearest designated safety zone?"

<ul class="player-options">
    <li>[[Look at Benny.]]</li>
    <li>[[Look at the sky.]]</li>
    <li>[[Look at the jungle.]]</li>
    <li>[["Lead the way."]]</li>
</ul>

:: Look at Benny.
Benny's exoskeleton is a soothing, pale pink.

Its carapace has a dull "matte" finish, while its limbs are slightly opalescent.

Its eyes: two gleaming black beads on tiny twitching stalks.

Benny's mouth in no way resembles that of a human, so its designers had to find other ways to anthropomorphize.

Benny emotes through exaggerated posture, like a silent cartoon character.

<<back>>


:: Look at the sky.
The sky is cloudless and blue, the local star directly overhead, pissing its rays down upon you. You sweat and scowl at it.

There is a grid of pale lines, half-finished but spanning a third of the sky. Construction up in orbit? Can't tell with the naked eye.

On the horizon are the coiled outlines of ''megastructures''. The organic-looking "grown" buildings that are the trademark of Redrock Corp.

<<back>>


:: Look at the jungle.
The jungle is a near-solid wall of green biota. Its base is a morass of strange fungi, moss, twisting vines. Some vines as thick as snakes. You get the feeling you could shove your arm into this and not get it back.

There is no getting through without a machete. Or a chainsaw.

Trees rise up from this tangle, their trunks at least a meter wide. Their branches intermesh to form a thick canopy: a second quagmire, looming high above the first.

<<back>>


:: "Lead the way."
"You got it, $player.pref! Let me see what the closest..." The robot pauses. It seems confused.

"Something wrong?"

"Yes. Strange. I can't seem to connect to RedNet for the latest satellite data. It's been a little while since I've checked in."

"How long?"

"About five-hundred solar days. Oh well. At least I have it cached!"